      "body": "Fixes #43116\n\n`QwenImageEditAdapter.pack` only packed `ref_latents[0]`. Extra reference images from ComfyUI's multi-image edit workflow were silently dropped.\n\nFix: pack every entry in `ref_latents`, concatenate along the token dimension, build `vae_image_sizes` as one entry per image. Matches the native pipeline's existing multi-ref handling in `configs/pipeline_configs/qwen_image.py`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added unit test `test_qwen_image_edit_pack_keeps_all_ref_latents` (CPU) in `test/unit/test_comfyui_adapters.py`, with 3 ref latents of different sizes.\n- Pre-fix: only 1 of 3 images kept (1024 tokens).\n- Post-fix: all 3 images kept (2368 tokens).\n- GPU: loaded real Qwen-Image-Edit-2511 on an A100, ran one forward pass with 3 ref latents through the patched adapter:\n  - `vae_image_sizes: [(64, 64), (96, 32), (48, 48)]`\n  - `image_latent` tokens: 2368\n  - `noise_pred` shape: `[1, 3600, 64]`, bf16\n  - No crash, no shape mismatch, all 3 images used.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37961882849](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37961882849)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37961882544](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37961882544)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37961882569](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37961882569)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
